2026-10-15T18:44:55 |On Thu, Mar 24, 2022 at 08:27:12AM -0600, Theo de Raadt wrote:
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> Miod Vallat <miod@online.fr> wrote:
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |>
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> > > I think we should reduce the number of zlibs in userland. Otherwise
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> > > security fixing becomes a nightmare. I will have a look at Perl.
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> >
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> > If you go this route, note that perl also contains a complete bzip2
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> > implementation. Since there has been concern, over a recent change
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> > proposed to tar, to only care about what's in base, we might want to
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> > add libbzip2 to base and link the perl module against it... (to be
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> > considered post-release)
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |>
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> And how many days or hours before someone says I want bzip2 support in
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> the bootblocks also (without any consideration their proposal blows up
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> 50% of the media, and will require a very significant amount of
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> development/test process).
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |>
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> I don't know why we limited ourselves to netinet. We should bring back
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> netiso. People should be able to depend upon is to supply them with
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |> choice even when it is irrelevant.
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |I don't want to start the discussion whether we want to import bzip2
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |into base.
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |The patch to use base zlib in Perl is rather simple. I am building
2026-10-15T18:44:55 |a release with it.
